#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; defines a filesystem hierarchy which is used by the &kde; environment "
"itself as well as all &kde; applications. In general &kde; stores all its "
"files in a directory tree with a fixed structure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default &kde; uses two directory trees:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One at the system level (for example <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/"
"kde3</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One at the user level in the user's home directory (usually <filename class="
"\"directory\"> ~/.kde</filename>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As a system administrator you can create additional trees. Such additional "
"trees can be used for <link linkend=\"user-profiles\">profiles</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "&SuSE; &Linux; for example uses:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>. (This is &SuSE;-"
"specific; other distributions may use <filename class=\"directory\">/usr</"
"filename> or <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/kde3</filename>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/etc/opt/kde3</filename>. (This was added by "
"&SuSE;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have the KIOSK Admin tool v0.7 or later installed you can check which "
"directory trees are used with the following command: "
"<userinput><command>kiosktool-kdedirs</command> <option>--check</option></"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; and &kde; applications look up files by scanning all the &kde; "
"directory trees. The directory trees are checked in order of precedence. "
"When a file is present in multiple directory trees, the file from the last "
"tree takes precedence. Normally, the tree located in the user's home "
"directory has the highest precedence. This is also the directory tree to "
"which changes are written."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information about the <literal>text/plain</literal> &MIME; type the "
"following files are searched:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user makes a change, the change is written to <filename class="
"\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop</"
"filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For configuration files the story is slightly different. If there are "
"multiple configuration files found in the directory trees with the same "
"name, their content is combined. The precedence order of the directory trees "
"plays a role here. When two files define the same configuration key, the "
"file with the highest precedence determines which value is used for the key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example, if the following two files exist, with these contents:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "The files will be merged to result in:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifying Directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Environment Variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example Setting(s)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "Comentari"

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEHOME"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.kde"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEROOTHOME"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "/root/.kde"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Different variable to prevent root writing to $KDEHOME of the user after "
"running <command>su</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEDIR"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:150 kde-for-admins.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>, <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/kde3</"
"filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Vendor dependent. Used by &kde; 2. If not set, falls back to compiled-in "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEDIRS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"New in &kde;3. Can list multiple locations separated by a colon. If not set, "
"falls back to $<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Don't <emphasis>need</emphasis> to be set, defaults work just fine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Running &kde;2 next to &kde;3? Point $<envar>KDEDIR</envar> to &kde; 2 and "
"$<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> to &kde; 3."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "A staff member at a university could have the following settings:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"KDEHOME='~/.kde3'\n"
"KDEROOTHOME='/root/.kde3'\n"
"KDEDIRS='/opt/kde_staff:/opt/kde3'"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Profiles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the previous example <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</"
"filename> contained additional settings and applications for staff members. "
"<quote>User Profiles</quote> allow you to add this directory only for "
"certain users and not for others. Add the following to <filename>/etc/kderc</"
"filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Directories-staff]\n"
"prefixes=/opt/kde_staff"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This creates a profile named <quote>staff</quote> that adds the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</filename> directory tree. (Note that "
"&SuSE; &Linux; uses <filename>/etc/kde3rc</filename> instead of <filename>/"
"etc/kderc</filename>. Now that we have a named profile it can be assigned to "
"users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To map profiles to users a mapping file needs to be specified in <filename>/"
"etc/kderc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Directories]\n"
"userProfileMapFile=/etc/kde-user-profile"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is now possible to assign a profile based on either the user name or "
"based on the &UNIX; group the user is part of."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To assign the staff profile to all users that are a member of the &UNIX; "
"group staff_members add the following to <filename>/etc/kde-user-profile</"
"filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[General]\n"
"groups=staff_members\n"
"[Groups]\n"
"staff_members=staff"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is also possible to assign a profile to a single user:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Users]\n"
"bastian=staff"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory Layout Revisited"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each directory tree used by &kde; has a fixed directory structure. "
"Directories that are not relevant for a certain tree, or simply not used can "
"be left out though. For example, directories used for temporary files are "
"usually only found under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</"
"envar></filename> but not in any other directory tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Architecture-specific Directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Architecture (OS and CPU type) specific directories:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>bin</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "Used for &kde; executables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>lib</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Used for &kde; libraries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "lib/kde3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains components, plugins, and other runtime loadable "
"objects for use by &kde; 3.<replaceable>x</replaceable> applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shared Directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shared: Not architecture specific, can be shared between different archs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/applnk"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files for &kde;-menu (old)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files for &kde;-menu (since "
"&kde; 3.2)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/apps"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Contains application-specific data files. Each application has a sub-"
"directory here for storing additional data files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/config"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configuration files. Configuration files are normally named after the "
"application they belong to plus the letters <quote>rc</quote>. A special "
"case is <filename>kdeglobals</filename>. This file is read by all &kde; "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/config/session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory is used by session management and is normally only available "
"under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar></filename>. At "
"the end of a session &kde; applications store their state here. The file "
"names consist of the name of the application followed by a number. The "
"session manager <command>ksmserver</command> stores references to these "
"numbers when saving a session in <filename>ksmserverrc</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/doc/HTML"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains documentation for &kde; applications. Documentation "
"is categorized by language and the application it belongs to. Normally at "
"least two files can be found in a directory: <filename>index.docbook</"
"filename>, which contains the documentation in the unformatted DocBook "
"format, and <filename>index.cache.bz2</filename>, which contains the same "
"documentation formatted as <command>bzip2</command>-compressed &HTML;. The "
"&HTML; version is used by &khelpcenter;. If the &HTML; version is missing, "
"&khelpcenter; will regenerate it from the DocBook version but this is a time-"
"consuming process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/icons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under this directory icons are stored. Icons are categorized by theme, "
"dimension and usage category."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/mimelnk"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this directory,<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files that "
"describe &MIME; types are stored. &kde; uses &MIME; types to identify the "
"type of a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/services"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files "
"that describe services. Services are like applications but are usually "
"launched by other applications instead of the user. Services do not appear "
"in the &kde; menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/servicetypes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files "
"that describe servicetypes. A servicetype usually represents a certain "
"programming interface. Applications and Services include in their <literal "
"role=\"extension\">>.desktop</literal> files the servicetypes that they "
"provide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/sounds"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "This directory contains sound files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains templates for creating files of various types. A "
"template consists of a <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file "
"that describes the file and that includes a reference to a file in the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">.source</filename> sub-directory. The "
"templates in this directory appear in the <guimenu>Create New</guimenu> menu "
"available on the desktop and in the file browser. When a user selects a "
"template from the menu its source file is copied."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/wallpapers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "This directory contains images that can be used as background picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "Host-specific Directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three host-specific directories that are usually symlinked to "
"other locations. If the directories do not already exist, the following "
"symlinks and directories will be created using the <command>lnusertemp</"
"command> utility:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/socket-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/ksocket-$<envar>USER</envar>/</"
"filename>, this is used for various &UNIX; sockets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/tmp-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/kde-$<envar>USER</envar>/</"
"filename>, this is used for temporary files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/cache-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp/kdecache-$<envar>USER</envar>/"
"</filename>, this is used for cached files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since both <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp</filename> and <filename class="
"\"directory\">/var/tmp</filename> are world writable, there is a possibility "
"that one of the above directories already exists but is owned by another "
"user. In that case the <command>lnusertemp</command> utility will create a "
"new directory with an alternative name and link to that instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Files"
msgstr "Fichièrs de configuracion"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; uses a simple text-based file format for all its configuration files. "
"It consists of key-value pairs that are placed in groups. All &kde; "
"configuration files use <acronym>UTF</acronym>-8 encoding for text outside "
"the <acronym>ASCII</acronym> range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The start of a group is indicated by a group name that is placed in square "
"brackets. All the key-value entries that follow belong to the group. The "
"group ends when either another group starts or when the end of the file is "
"reached. Entries at the top of the file that are not preceded by a group "
"name belong to the default group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following example shows a configuration file that consists of two "
"groups. The first group contains the keys <varname>LargeCursor</varname> and "
"<varname>SingleClick</varname>, the second group contains the keys "
"<varname>Show hidden files</varname> and <varname>Sort by</varname>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE]\n"
"LargeCursor=false\n"
"SingleClick=true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KFileDialog Settings]\n"
"Show hidden files=false\n"
"Sort by=Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entries in a group consist of a key and value separated by an equals sign. "
"The key can contain spaces and may be followed by options placed in square "
"brackets. The part after the equals sign is the value of the entry. Any "
"white space surrounding the equals sign is ignored, as is any trailing white "
"space. Put more concisely, the format is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "<replaceable>entry</replaceable>=<replaceable>value</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a value is supposed to include a space at the begin or end then this can "
"be achieved by using a backslash followed by an <quote>s</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several other backslash codes; here is a complete list:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\s</token> can be used as space"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\t</token> can be used to include a tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\r</token> for a carriage return character"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\n</token> for a linefeed character (new line)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\\\</token> to include the backslash itself"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> entry "
"starts with two spaces while the <varname>Description</varname> entry "
"contains three lines of text. Linefeeds in backslash notation are used to "
"separate the different lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=\\s My Caption\n"
"Description=This is\\na very long\\ndescription."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Empty lines in configuration files are ignored, as are lines that start with "
"a hash mark (<quote>#</quote>). The hash mark can be used to add comments to "
"configuration files. It should be noted that when a &kde; application "
"updates a configuration file the comments are <emphasis>not</emphasis> "
"preserved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There can be multiple configuration files with the same name in the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">share/config</filename> sub-directory of the "
"various &kde; directory trees. In this case the information of all these "
"configuration files is combined on a key-by-key basis. If the same key "
"within a certain group is defined in more than one place, the key value read "
"from the directory tree with the highest precedence will be used. "
"Configuration files under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</"
"envar></filename> always have the highest precedence. If a key in a certain "
"group is defined multiple times in a single file, the value of the last "
"entry is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</"
"filename> contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Position=20,20\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=20,20"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To prevent users being able to override default settings, settings can be "
"marked immutable. Settings can be made immutable individually, per group or "
"per file. An individual entry can be locked down by adding <userinput>[$i]</"
"userinput> behind the key, &eg;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color[$i]=blue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A group of entries can be locked down by placing <userinput>[$i]</userinput> "
"behind the group name, &eg;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid "[MyGroup][$i]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To lock down the entire file, start the file with <userinput>[$i]</"
"userinput> on a single line, &ie;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "[$i]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</"
"filename> contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So-called <quote>Shell Expansion</quote> can be used to provide more dynamic "
"default values. With shell expansion the value of a configuration key can be "
"constructed from the value of an environment variable or from the output of "
"a shell command. To enable shell expansion for a configuration entry, the "
"key must be followed by <token>[$e]</token>. Normally the expanded form is "
"written into the user's configuration file after first use. To prevent that, "
"it is recommend to lock the configuration entry down by using <token>[$ie]</"
"token>. The user can't change it then of course."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value for the <varname>Host</varname> entry is "
"determined by the output of the <command>hostname</command> program. This "
"setting is also locked down to ensure that the value is always determined "
"dynamically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value for the <varname>Email</varname> entry is determined by filling in "
"the values of the $<envar>USER</envar> and $<envar>HOST</envar> environment "
"variables. When <systemitem class=\"username\">joe</systemitem> is logged in "
"on <systemitem class=\"systemname\">joes_host</systemitem> this will result "
"in a value equal to <literal>joe@joes_host</literal>. The setting is not "
"locked down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Mail Settings] \n"
"Host[$ie]=$(hostname)\n"
"Email[$e]=${USER}@${HOST}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most configuration entries can be indexed with a language code. In this "
"case, the language that the user has selected for use on the desktop is used "
"to look up the key value. If the default language (American English) has "
"been selected or if there is no index that corresponds to the selected "
"language, the key entry without index is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> entry "
"depends on the language. If the user has selected French as language "
"(language code <literal>fr</literal>) the value of the entry will be "
"<quote>Ma L&eacute;gende</quote>. In all other cases the value <quote>My "
"Caption</quote> will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:607 kde-for-admins.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=My Caption\n"
"Caption[fr]=Ma L&eacute;gende"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> entry depends on "
"the language. If the user has selected French as language (language code "
"<literal>fr</literal>) the value of the entry will be <quote>Ma L&eacute;"
"gende.</quote> In all other cases the value <quote>My Caption</quote> will "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In general the entries that can appear in a configuration file are not "
"documented. With &kde; 3.2 a start has been made to change this. In "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config.kcfg</"
"filename>, files can be found that provide a formal description of the "
"possible entries in a configuration file. These are used by the new &kde; "
"Configuration Editor when available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is an example &XML; configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?&gt;\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE kcfg SYSTEM \"http://www.kde.org/standards/kcfg/1.0/kcfg.dtd"
"\"&gt;\n"
"&lt;kcfg&gt;\n"
"    &lt;kcfgfile name=\"korganizerrc\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;group name=\"General\"&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Bool\" key=\"Auto Save\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;label&gt;Enable automatic saving of calendar&lt;/label&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;true&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Int\" key=\"Auto Save Interval\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;10&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"&lt;/kcfg&gt;\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "It has the same effect as:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[General]\n"
"Auto Save=false\n"
"Auto Save Interval=25"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; Startup Sequence"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always runs as <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>! Uses "
"<filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdmrc</filename> and "
"<filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xservers</filename>. The latter contains entries like:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ":0 local /usr/X11R6/bin/X :0 vt07"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "Relevant startup files are also:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid "[X-*-Core] section in <filename>kdmrc</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setup - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsetup</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "User enters username &amp; password"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid "Startup - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xstartup</filename> - prepare as root"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Session - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsession</filename> - starts session as user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"= For a KDE session: <command>kde</command> or <command>startkde</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"= If present <filename>~/.xsession</filename> or <filename>~/.xinitrc</"
"filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reset - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xreset</filename> - after session finished"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Startup Script: <command>startkde</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; startup sequence starts with the <filename>startkde</filename> "
"script. In most cases this script gets called from the display manager "
"(&kdm;) once the user has been authenticated. Their are two very important "
"lines in the <filename>startkde</filename> script:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"LD_BIND_NOW=true kdeinit4 +kcminit_startup and kwrapper4 ksmserver $KDEWM"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first line starts the <command>kdeinit4</command> master process. The "
"<command>kdeinit4</command> master process is used to start all other &kde; "
"processes. It show up in the output of <command>ps <option>aux</option></"
"command> as <computeroutput>kdeinit4: Running...</computeroutput>. The "
"arguments after <command>kdeinit4</command> are the names of additional "
"processes to be started. The <token>+</token> indicates that "
"<command>kdeinit4</command> needs to wait till the process has finished. "
"<command>kdeinit4</command> also starts <command>klauncher</command> and "
"<command>kded</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second of the two lines asks <command>kdeinit4</command> to start the "
"<command>ksmserver</command> session manager process. The session manager "
"determines the lifetime of the session. When this process exits, the user is "
"logged out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background Processes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All &kde; background services are user-specific: unlike system daemons they "
"are not shared between users. As well as being unique per user they are also "
"unique per X-server display. The processes are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "dcopserver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid "Desktop communication"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "kded"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generic service daemon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Triggers <link linkend=\"ksycoca\">Sycoca</link> database updates when needed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kcminit</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "Initialization service"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:736
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"kcminit\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:741 kde-for-admins.docbook:817
#, no-c-format
msgid "klauncher"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Program launch (this is <emphasis>not</emphasis> the <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap> </keycombo>dialog!)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"klauncher\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:750 kde-for-admins.docbook:838
#, no-c-format
msgid "knotify"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "User notifications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"knotify\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid "ksmserver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:758
#, no-c-format
msgid "Session management"
msgstr "Gestion de session"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"ksmserver\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdeinit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdeinit</command> is used to start all other &kde; programs. "
"<command>kdeinit</command> can start normal binary program files as well as "
"<command>kdeinit</command> loadable modules (<acronym>KLM</acronym>s). "
"<acronym>KLM</acronym>s work just like binary program files but can be "
"started more efficiently. <acronym>KLM</acronym>s live in <filename class="
"\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/lib/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:775 kde-for-admins.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The drawback is that programs started this way appear as "
"<computeroutput><command>kdeinit</command></computeroutput> in the output of "
"<command>top</command> and <command>ps</command>. Use <command>top <option>-"
"c</option></command> or <command>ps <option>aux</option></command> to see "
"the actual program name:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt><userinput><command>ps <option>aux</option></command></"
"userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"waba     23184  0.2  2.1 23428 11124 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit4: "
"Running...\n"
"waba     23189  0.2  2.4 25136 12496 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit4: "
"klauncher\n"
"waba     23192  0.7  2.8 25596 14772 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit4: "
"kded\n"
"waba     23203  0.8  3.4 31516 17892 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit4: "
"knotify\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:783
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>kdeinit: Running...</computeroutput> indicates the master "
"<command>kdeinit</command> process. The other processes listed are programs "
"started as <acronym>KLM</acronym>s."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:787
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When <command>kdeinit</command> starts for the first time it will launch "
"<command>klauncher</command>, and <command>kded</command>, as well as any "
"additional programs specified on its command line in the <command>startkde</"
"command> script, normally <command>kcminit_startup</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>kcminit</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:798
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kcminit</command> executes initialization services during startup. "
"Initialization services are specified in the .desktop files of applications "
"or services via the <varname>X-KDE-Init</varname> line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8\n"
"Exec=kcmshell energy\n"
"Icon=energy_star\n"
"Type=Application\n"
"X-KDE-Library=energy\n"
"X-KDE-Init=energy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:804
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Initialization services are typically used for initializing hardware based "
"on user-specified settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kcminit <option>--list</option></command></userinput> "
"can be used to show all initialization services and "
"<userinput><command>kcminit <replaceable>service</replaceable></command></"
"userinput> can be used to execute a single service explicitly. This can be "
"useful when investigating startup problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:819
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>klauncher</command> is a daemon which is responsible for service "
"activation within &kde;. It operates in close connection with the "
"<command>kdeinit</command> master process to start new processes. &kde; "
"applications communicate with <command>klauncher</command> over &DCOP; in "
"order to start new applications or services."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:825
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Best known from the error message: <computeroutput><errortext> KLauncher "
"could not be reached via DBus </errortext></computeroutput> which either "
"indicates a serious problem with the <command>dcopserver</command> or that "
"<command>klauncher</command> crashed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:830
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>klauncher</command> can be restarted by restarting "
"<command>kdeinit</command> from a console window. Make sure that "
"$<envar>HOME</envar>, $<envar>DISPLAY</envar> and the various $<envar>KDEDIR"
"(S)</envar> are set correctly when doing so!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The primary task of <command>knotify</command> is to relay sound "
"notifications to the sound server, it also provides alternative notification "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:850
#, no-c-format
msgid "KSMServer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:852
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>ksmserver</command> is &kde;'s session manager. On startup the "
"session manager launches auto-start applications and restores applications "
"from the previous session. The applications to auto-start are indicated by "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files in the <filename class="
"\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/autostart</filename> directory. "
"Whether or not to auto-start an application can be made conditional upon "
"some configuration entry determined by the <varname>X-KDE-autostart-"
"condition</varname> entry in the <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</"
"literal> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:864
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <filename>ktip.desktop</filename> file for example contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid "X-KDE-autostart-condition=ktiprc:TipOfDay:RunOnStart:true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This means that the <filename>ktiprc</filename> configuration file is "
"checked for a <varname>RunOnStart</varname> entry in the <varname>[TipOfDay]"
"</varname> section. If no such entry is found, <literal>true</literal> is "
"assumed, which means that <application>ktip</application> is one of the "
"applications that is auto-started by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of the applications auto-started by <command>ksmserver</command> are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdesktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kicker;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:890
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:895
#, no-c-format
msgid "ktip"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid "A tip of the day program"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid "kwrited"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid "A utility to receive system messages sent to the user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid "&klipper;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:908
#, no-c-format
msgid "A clipboard utility that docks in the panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid "kalarm"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:914
#, no-c-format
msgid "A utility that warns about upcoming events and appointments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdesktop</command> in its turn automatically starts applications "
"stored in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/Autostart</"
"filename>. <command>kdesktop</command> will automatically open any files "
"stored in this directory including documents, binary files or applications "
"in the form of <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:927
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; session manager also restores one of the previous sessions. A "
"session contains a collection of applications as well as application-"
"specific information that reflects the state of the applications at the time "
"the session was saved. Sessions are stored in the <filename>ksmserverrc</"
"filename> configuration file which contains references to application-"
"specific state information. The application-specific state information is "
"saved in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/share/config/"
"session</filename>. The state information of &kwin; contains the location of "
"the application windows of all the other applications in the session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some important environment variables used by &kde;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:949
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Has to be set if <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> is not set and has to point to the "
"root of the &kde; installation tree. Allows &kde; to find its data like "
"icons, menus and libraries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEDIRS</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Overrides <envar>KDEDIR</envar> and allows you to specify multiple "
"directories where &kde; searches for its data. Useful if you want or have to "
"install some programs to a different prefix than the rest of &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:965
#, no-c-format
msgid "$KDEHOME"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:965
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not set, &kde; uses <filename class=\"directory\">~/.kde</filename> as "
"the directory where personal data is stored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEROOTHOME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not set, &kde; uses <filename class=\"directory\">~root/.kde</filename> "
"as the directory for <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>'s "
"personal data. Was introduced to prevent &kde; from accidently overwriting "
"user data with root permissions when the user runs a &kde; program after "
"switching with <command>su</command> to <systemitem class=\"username\">root</"
"systemitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEWM</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <envar>KDEWM</envar> environment variable has been set, then it will "
"be used as &kde;'s window manager within the <command>startkde</command> "
"script instead of &kwin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:988
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_LANG</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:988
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Overrides the &kde; language configuration, &eg; <userinput>KDE_LANG=fr "
"kprogram &amp;</userinput> starts a program with French translation if the "
"necessary files are installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:995
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_MULTIHEAD</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:995
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set this variable to <literal>true</literal> to indicate that &kde; is "
"running on a multi-head system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_FORK_SLAVES</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1002
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2.3) Set this variable to spawn <acronym>KIO</acronym>-slaves "
"directly from the application process itself. By default <acronym>KIO</"
"acronym>-slaves are spawned using <command>klauncher</command>/"
"<command>kdeinit</command>. This option is useful if the <acronym>KIO</"
"acronym>-slave should run in the same environment as the application. This "
"can be the case with <application>Clearcase</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1012
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_HOME_READONLY</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1013
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set this variable to indicate that your home directory is mounted as read-"
"only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1018
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_NO_IPV6</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1018
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2.3) - Set this variable to disable <acronym>IPv6</acronym> "
"support and <acronym>IPv6</acronym> <acronym>DNS</acronym> lookups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_IS_PRELINKED</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) - Set this variable to indicate that you have prelinked "
"your &kde; binaries and libraries. This will turn off <command>kdeinit</"
"command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1032
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_UTF8_FILENAMES</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1032
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this environment variable is set, &kde; assumes all filenames are in "
"<acronym>UTF-8</acronym> encoding regardless of the current C locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1039
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_FULL_SESSION</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1039
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Automatically set to true by &kde; startup, it is used by "
"&eg; &konqueror; to know if it should consider remaining in memory for "
"future re-use when being closed. If not set, &konqueror; will exit after "
"being closed (&eg; &kdesu; does that, it's also useful for debugging)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDESYCOCA</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to specify the path and the name of the generated &kde; system "
"configuration cache file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDETMP</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows to specify another path than <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp</"
"filename> where &kde; stores its temporary files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEVARTMP</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows to specify another path than <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp</"
"filename> where &kde; stores its variable files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Defines the base directory relative to which user-specific "
"data files should be stored. Default is <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.local/share</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Defines the preference-ordered set of base directories to "
"search for data files in addition to the <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar></filename> base directory. Default is "
"<literal>/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/</literal>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1082
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; adds locations from $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> and profiles as well. Used "
"for <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> and <literal role="
"\"extension\">.directory</literal> menu files. <literal role=\"extension\">."
"desktop</literal> files under <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>/applications</filename>. <literal role="
"\"extension\">.directory</literal> files under $XDG_DATA_DIRS/desktop-"
"directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1094
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1094
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(&kde; 3.2) - Defines the base directory relative to which user specific "
"configuration files should be stored. Default is <filename class=\"directory"
"\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.config</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1101
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</envar>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(&kde; 3.2) - Defines the preference-ordered set of base directories to "
"search for configuration files in addition to the $<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</"
"envar> base directory. The default is <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/"
"xdg</filename> &kde; adds locations from $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> and "
"profiles as well. Used by <literal role=\"extension\">.menu</literal> "
"descriptions in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</"
"envar>/menus</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1115
#, no-c-format
msgid "The kdeinit Mystery"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdeinit</command> is used to start all other &kde; programs. "
"<command>kdeinit</command> can start normal binary program f iles as well as "
"<command>kdeinit</command> loadable modules (<acronym>KLM</acronym>s). "
"<acronym>KLM</acronym>s work just like binary program files but can be "
"started more efficiently. <acronym>KLM</acronym>s live in <filename class="
"\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/lib/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>ps aux | grep bastian</command></"
"userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"bastian  26061  0.0  2.2 24284 11492 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"Running...\n"
"bastian  26064  0.0  2.2 24036 11524 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"dcopserver\n"
"bastian  26066  0.1  2.5 26056 12988 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klauncher\n"
"bastian  26069  0.4  3.2 27356 16744 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"kded\n"
"bastian  26161  0.2  2.7 25344 14096 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"ksmserver\n"
"bastian  26179  1.1  3.4 29716 17812 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"kicker\n"
"bastian  26192  0.4  3.0 26776 15452 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klipper\n"
"bastian  26195  1.0  3.5 29200 18368 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"kdesktop\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you might have noticed, this has another side effect, making it difficult "
"to kill a process that is causing trouble:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>killall kdesktop</command></"
"userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>kdesktop: no process killed</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You might be tempted to try <userinput><command>killall kdeinit</command></"
"userinput>, but killing all kdeinit processes will have the effect of "
"shutting down all of &kde;. In effect, total destruction!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two simple solutions to this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kdekillall kdesktop</command></"
"userinput>\n"
"or good old\n"
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kill 26195</command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdekillall</command> is part of the &kde; <acronym>SDK</acronym> "
"package."
msgstr ""

