#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kde; 3.2 a common menu format is introduced at <ulink url=\"http://"
"freedesktop.org/Standards/menu-spec/\">http://freedesktop.org/Standards/menu-"
"spec/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before &kde; 3.2:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Directory structure under <filename class=\"directory\">share/applnk</"
"filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1402
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory structure represents menu structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file represents a single "
"application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It was difficult to rearrange the structure in &kde; 3.2 so the new menu "
"format:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1414
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defines structure in a single .menu file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Is based on categories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1416
#, no-c-format
msgid "is shared between <acronym>GNOME</acronym> and &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supports applnk style menus as well"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1422 kde-for-admins.docbook:1484
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example from <filename>applications.menu</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"        &lt;Menu&gt;\n"
"            &lt;Name&gt;Office&lt;/Name&gt;\n"
"            &lt;Directory&gt;suse-office.directory&lt;/Directory&gt;\n"
"            &lt;Include&gt;\n"
"                &lt;Filename&gt;Acrobat Reader.desktop&lt;/Filename&gt;\n"
"                &lt;Filename&gt;kde-kpresenter.desktop&lt;/Filename&gt;\n"
"                &lt;Filename&gt;kde-kword.desktop&lt;/Filename&gt;\n"
"            &lt;/Include&gt;\n"
"        &lt;Menu&gt;\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu entry with 3 applications:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1428
#, no-c-format
msgid "/usr/share/applications/Acrobat Reader.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1431
#, no-c-format
msgid "/opt/kde3/share/applications/kde/kpresenter.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1433
#, no-c-format
msgid "/opt/kde3/share/applications/kde/kword.desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1441
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stored Where?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.menu</literal> files describing the menu "
"structure. The files are stored in <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/etc/xdg/menus</filename> and <filename class="
"\"directory\">/etc/xdg/menus</filename>. These store the system-wide menu "
"structure and are controlled by $<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</envar>. <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.config/menus</filename> stores "
"user-specific changes to the menu structure and is controlled by "
"$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</envar>. For more information, see <ulink url="
"\"http://www.freedesktop.org/Standards/basedir-spec\">http://www.freedesktop."
"org/Standards/basedir-spec</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files describe the "
"applications and are stored in: <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/applications</filename>, <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr/share/applications</filename>, <filename class=\"directory"
"\">/usr/local/share/applications</filename>. These are the system-wide "
"application <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files which are "
"controlled by $<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.local/applications</"
"filename> contains user-specific <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</"
"literal> files and user-specific changes. It is controlled by "
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>. For more information, see <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.freedesktop.org/Standards/basedir-spec\">http://www.freedesktop.org/"
"Standards/basedir-spec</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.directory</literal> files describing the sub-"
"menus are stored in: <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"share/desktop-directories</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/"
"share/desktop-directories</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/"
"local/share/desktop-directories</filename>. These are the system-wide menu "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.directory</literal> files, controlled by "
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>. The user-specific changes are stored in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.local/desktop-"
"directories</filename>. These are controlled by $<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</"
"envar>. For more information, see <ulink url=\"http://www.freedesktop.org/"
"Standards/basedir-spec\">http://www.freedesktop.org/Standards/basedir-spec</"
"ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"             &lt;Menu&gt;\n"
"                        &lt;Name&gt;Art&lt;/Name&gt;\n"
"                        &lt;Directory&gt;suse-edutainment-art.directory&lt;/"
"Directory&gt;\n"
"                        &lt;Include&gt;\n"
"                                &lt;Category&gt;X-SuSE-Art&lt;/Category&gt;\n"
"                        &lt;/Include&gt;\n"
"                &lt;/Menu&gt;\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>Art</literal> is the internal name for this menu. <filename>suse-"
"edutainment-art.directory</filename> defines the name and icon for this "
"menu, and the menu includes all applications that have <literal>X-SuSE-Art</"
"literal> listed as a category, &eg;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1492
#, no-c-format
msgid "Categories=Qt;KDE;Education;X-SuSE-Art"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>suse-edutainment-art.directory</filename> defines the name and "
"icon for this menu:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1496
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Name=Art and Culture\n"
"Icon=kcmsystem"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1502
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications <emphasis>not</emphasis> in the menu do <emphasis>not</"
"emphasis> exist with regard to other applications or file associations: If "
"you remove an application from the menu, &kde; assumes you don't want to use "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When applications are unwanted in the menu, either place them in <filename>."
"hidden</filename> menu or a dedicated menu with <programlisting>\n"
"NoDisplay=true\n"
"</programlisting> in the <literal role=\"extension\">.directory</literal> "
"file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1515
#, no-c-format
msgid "Essential Menus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/etc/xdg/menus/"
"applications-merged/</filename> contains <filename>kde-essential.menu</"
"filename> which includes some essential menus that are normally not shown in "
"the &kde; menu itself:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Control Center has a hidden Settings menu whose contents are defined by "
"<filename>kde-settings.menu</filename> and whose icon and name are defined "
"by <filename>kde-settings.directory</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Info Center has a hidden Information menu whose contents are defined by "
"<filename>kde-information.menu</filename> and whose icon and name are "
"defined by <filename>kde-information.directory</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Screensavers contains a hidden System/Screensavers menu, whose contents are "
"defined by <filename>kde-screensavers.menu</filename> and whose icon and "
"name are defined by <filename>kde-system-screensavers.directory</filename>. "
"<filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/desktop-directories/kde-system-"
"screensavers.directory</filename> contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1538
#, no-c-format
msgid "NoDisplay=true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1545
#, no-c-format
msgid "Old-Style Menus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; continues to support old-style menus that are defined by the directory "
"structures in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/"
"applnk</filename> (system wide) and <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/applnk</filename> (user specific). This is "
"observed unless the <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file has "
"a <varname>Categories</varname>= line. In that case the categories determine "
"the location in the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: application
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1556
#, no-c-format
msgid "KSycoca"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>KSycoca</application> caches menu structure and information "
"about all available applications. You can rebuild the database with "
"<userinput><command>kbuildsycoca4</command></userinput>. The database which "
"is built lives in <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp/kdecache-"
"${<envar>USER</envar>}/ksycoca</filename>. It is automatically updated by "
"<application>KDED</application>, checked during &kde; login, and "
"<application>KDED</application> watches for changes while logged in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To disable watching for changes (since it may hurt over NFS) add the "
"following to <filename>kdedrc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[General]\n"
"CheckSycoca=false"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1572
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To force regeneration, run <userinput><command>touch $<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"share/services/update_ksycoca</command></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1577
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmenuedit;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmenuedit; is aimed at a single user setup. Changes to menu structure are "
"saved to <filename>~/.config/menus/applications-kmenuedit.menu</filename>, "
"changes to applications are saved in <filename class=\"directory\">~/.local/"
"share/applications/</filename> and changes to sub-menus (icon, name) are "
"saved in <filename class=\"directory\">~/.local/share/desktop-directories/</"
"filename>. The KIOSK Admin Tool uses &kmenuedit; and copies the above "
"changes to profile- or system-wide locations."
msgstr ""

